id: pm-rust-1ycz
title: Match published container readiness for cyclic parent graphs
description: "Round 2 readiness-index review found a pre-existing parity gap. In a real disposable tracker with one open Task whose stored parent equals its own ID, published 2026.10.14 claim --next exits 3 with no_available_next_item; native exits 0 and claims it. Published hasOpenDescendant recognizes the nonterminal node reached through the cycle, while the existing native descendant check explicitly excludes the root. The performance-only indexing change retains prior case and cycle behavior. Repair cyclic-container semantics in separate differential work, including self cycles and mixed terminal/nonterminal cycles, without restoring repeated corpus scans."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[2]: conformance,selection
created_at: "2026-10-14T10:44:14.727Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-15T03:52:50.272Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-15T03:52:50.254Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-15T03:52:50.254Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: Real cyclic tracker differentials match published exit/stdout/stderr and durable state; indexing remains bounded and its deterministic scan regression passes
parent: pm-rust-u4al
resolution: "Fixed in pm-rust#81: Match published container readiness for cyclic parent graphs"
expected_result: "The native implementation matches the pinned PM CLI oracle for: Match published container readiness for cyclic parent graphs"
actual_result: "The differential oracle tests for this item pass in the merged head on Linux, macOS and Windows, and each fix's regression test fails when reverted (recorded in the item's comments)."
comments[5]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-14T20:34:41.851Z",codex-agent,"Implementing the native parity batch against the locked 2026.10.14 oracle. Evidence will compare real disposable trackers, complete output envelopes and durable artifacts, with a behavioral revert proof and unchanged release gates."
  "2026-10-14T20:43:01.763Z",codex-agent,"Regression proof on the unchanged main behavior: cargo test --locked --test claim_release_differential cyclic_parent_readiness_matches_published -- --nocapture failed with native exit 0 versus oracle exit 3 on a self-parent cycle. After the index fix, the same test passes for self cycles, mixed terminal cycles, active cycles and all-terminal cycles. Witnesses now start at parent edges so only cyclic reachability includes the candidate itself; the bounded corpus index remains in use."
  "2026-10-14T21:33:35.804Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof: cargo test --locked --test claim_release_differential cyclic_parent_readiness_matches_published -- --exact --nocapture compiled and failed at runtime with exit 101. Restoring the prior readiness functions claims a self-parent item: native exit 0 versus oracle exit 3. The regression test stayed in place, and all source bytes were restored after the check."
  "2026-10-14T22:40:24.377Z",codex-agent,"The item-linked pinned-oracle command passed through pm test --run --only-last --progress --fail-on-skipped --fail-on-empty-test-run --json: 1 tests passed, zero failures or skips. Test-result tracking is disabled by project policy, so this append-only comment records the observed receipt. The behavioral revert failure is recorded separately."
  "2026-10-15T00:40:07.758Z",codex-agent,"Final Linux acceptance: just release-check passed at unchanged pins and thresholds in an isolated Git identity environment. Both the ordinary and fresh branch-instrumented suites passed 317 tests across 17 targets, with zero failures or ignored tests. Coverage: 5646/5646 lines, 8630/8630 regions, 522/522 functions and 1194/1194 branches, all 100 percent. Formatting, deny-warnings Clippy, private-item rustdoc, identity audit, locked-oracle differential suites, cargo audit and changelog check passed. Cargo audit retains the inherited allowed RUSTSEC-2024-0449 unmaintained advisory. Per-item behavioral revert proof and linked-test receipts remain recorded separately. Releasing ownership for orchestrator verification; this item remains in progress and is not closed."
